## Creational Patterns
Creational various object creation mechanisms, which increase flexability and reuse existing code.

### 1) Factory Method
  - Provides a interface
  - Creates objects in a super class
  - Allows subclasses to change the object being created

### 2) Abstract Factory
  - Create families of the same object
  - Don't need to specify their concrete classes

### 3) Builder
  - Construct complex objects step by step
  - Produce different types and representations of a object using the same construction code

### 4) Prototype
  - Copy existing objects without depending on the classes

### 5) Singleton
  - Only on instance of a class exists
  - Provides a global access point to the class
